  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "Twi 'nnɔn {h}' (o'clock), additive 'nnɔn {h} ne sima N' for :05-:25, 'nnɔn {h} ne fa' (half), and the subtractive idiom 'aka sima N na abɔ nnɔn {next_h}' (N minutes remain before it strikes next hour) for :35-:55. Hour 12 fixed from truncated 'dumien' to 'dumienu'. Standard 12-hour count (Ghana does not use a 6 a.m.-based count). Minutes word 'sima' (variant 'simma'); 'ne' (and) chosen over the idiom 'apa ho' because it is unambiguous either way."
    }
  ]
